class BetIntelligence(TypedDict, total=False):
    bet_type: Optional[str]
    """Canonical bet token, e.g. ML_HOME/ML_AWAY/ML_DRAW (soccer), ML_P1/ML_P2 (head-to-head sports), SPREAD_HOME/SPREAD_AWAY, OVER, UNDER."""
    player_role: Optional[str]
    """'home'/'away' for team sports or 'p1'/'p2' for head-to-head sports. Null for match-level tokens (OVER, UNDER, ML_DRAW), which are not about either side."""
    player_id: Optional[int]
    """Player ID when this bet is about an individual player; null for team bets and match-level tokens (OVER, UNDER, ML_DRAW)."""
    team_id: Optional[int]
    """Team ID when this bet is about a team; null for individual-player bets and match-level tokens (OVER, UNDER, ML_DRAW). A draw is not a bet on either team, so ML_DRAW carries no team_id — safe to sum exposure by team_id across bets without double-counting the draw."""
    player_name: Optional[str]
    """Display name of the player or team this bet is about; null for match-level tokens (OVER, UNDER, ML_DRAW). Duplicates `players[player_role].name` for convenience when flattening bets[]."""
    market: Optional[Dict[str, Any]]
    """Market quote used for this bet: {price: American odds, line: handicap/total line or null for moneyline, book: bookmaker slug when known}. For predictive-framework sports `book` is always populated from the assessment; for legacy sports it may be omitted. Present for every sport."""
    computed_at: Optional[str]
    """ISO-8601 UTC timestamp of when this bet's numbers last materially changed — not when they were last checked. The publisher re-runs on a schedule but only rewrites a row when the price, line, or probability moves beyond a tolerance, so an older `computed_at` means 'unchanged since', not 'stale'. Values legitimately differ between bets on the same event because each market moves independently."""
    tier: Optional[str]
    """Recommendation tier: 'very_high', 'strong', 'moderate', or 'avoid'. Null whenever `edge` is null — a tier ranks a bet against its price."""
    confidence_score: Optional[float]
    """Not published. Use `probability`."""
    confidence_score_pre_validator: Optional[float]
    """Not published."""
    coverage: Optional[float]
    """Not published."""
    signals: Optional[Dict[str, Any]]
    """Not published."""
    validator: Optional[Dict[str, Any]]
    """Not published."""
    narrative: Optional[str]
    """Not published."""
    rationale: List[str]
    """Not published. Event-level context chips live on the top-level `rationale` of IntelligenceResponse."""
    attribution: List[str]
    """Not published."""
    probability: Optional[float]
    """Published probability for this outcome, 0-1. Outcomes of the same market (e.g. ML_HOME + ML_DRAW + ML_AWAY) sum to 1. Present on the customer surface for MLB, soccer, and tennis."""
    interval: Optional[List[float]]
    """[lo, hi] band around `probability`, 0-1. Read it as 'how much evidence backs this number', not as a statistical confidence interval. A freshly-opened, unmoved line gets a wider band than a heavily-traded one. Thin evidence widens this band rather than removing the response. Present on the customer surface for MLB, soccer, and tennis."""
    p_model: Optional[float]
    """Internal — omitted from customer payloads (MLB/soccer/tennis). Fitted model probability before blending with the market."""
    p_market: Optional[float]
    """Internal — omitted from customer payloads (MLB/soccer/tennis). De-vigged market probability before blending; use `probability` / `fair_price` instead."""
    blend_w: Optional[float]
    """Internal — omitted from customer payloads (MLB/soccer/tennis). Weight on the model when blending with the market."""
    fair_price: Optional[int]
    """American-odds fair price implied by `probability` — the vig-free line. Comparing it to `market.price` gives the bookmaker's margin on this side. Predictive-framework sports only."""
    edge: Optional[float]
    """Expected profit per 1 unit staked at `market.price`, i.e. `probability x decimal_odds - 1`. Positive means the price pays more than the probability justifies. Null when no model-backed edge is published (current MLB/soccer/tennis Stage 1). Present on the customer surface — null today, reserved for future recommend gating."""
    sufficiency: Optional[float]
    """Internal — omitted from customer payloads (MLB/soccer/tennis). Evidence strength 0-1 used internally to set interval width."""
    phase: Optional[str]
    """Internal — omitted from customer payloads (MLB/soccer/tennis). Pipeline stage (`quant` / `full`)."""
    model_version: Optional[str]
    """Internal — omitted from customer payloads (MLB/soccer/tennis). Parameter-set identifier for traceability."""
    drivers: List[Dict[str, Any]]
    """Internal — omitted from customer payloads (MLB/soccer/tennis). Signed contributions to probability used in the assessment pipeline."""
    alignment: Optional[Dict[str, Any]]
    """Internal — omitted from customer payloads (MLB/soccer/tennis). Qualitative-overlay agreement detail."""
    fair: Optional[Dict[str, Any]]
    """Sharp-consensus fair price for this outcome: {probability, books, n_books, is_consensus}. `probability` is distinct from `p_market` (the *priced* book's own de-vigged probability) and from `fair_price` (American odds implied by the published `probability`, above) — it is the sharp-book reference a cross-book price gap is measured against (MLS: Pinnacle / `SOCCER_SHARP_BOOKS`; MLB: Pinnacle+Circa / `MLB_SHARP_BOOKS`). `is_consensus` is false whenever `n_books` < 2. Populated for MLS and MLB; null for other leagues until their market plane is wired. Predictive-framework sports only."""
    edges_by_book: Optional[Dict[str, Any]]
    """Price gap versus the sharp-reference fair probability (`fair.probability`), keyed by bookmaker — `fair.probability × decimal_odds − 1` at each book's posted price. A line-shopping metric: rank soft books by these gaps (largest gap = furthest above the sharp reference). Populated for MLS (retail soft books for Price — Edge archive stays FanDuel/Hard Rock) and MLB (retail soft books: DK/FD/BetMGM/Caesars/Bet365/Hard Rock/BetOnline — Price surface; Edge allowlist remains independence-cleared DK/FD only). Null for other leagues or markets with no soft quote. Predictive-framework sports only."""
    best: Optional[Dict[str, Any]]
    """Highest price-gap book across `edges_by_book`: {book, price, edge, quote_age_seconds}. Same metric as `edges_by_book`: price gap versus a de-vigged sharp reference. On MLB, `best_*` is Tier C / informational line-shopping even when the gap is positive (DK/FD ML and RL/totals are hard-null for Edge). Use `best.book`/`best.price` as the line-shopping target. `quote_age_seconds` is `best.book`'s posted-price age at publish — quotes older than 30 minutes are excluded. Populated for MLS and MLB; null otherwise or when `edges_by_book` is empty. Predictive-framework sports only."""
    ev: Optional[Dict[str, Any]]
    """**Beta.** Customer-facing expected-value estimate: {beta: true, book, price, ev_pct, kelly_fraction, quote_age_seconds, n_books}. `ev_pct` is the selected book's price gap × 100 (`fair.probability × decimal − 1`); `kelly_fraction` is the full-Kelly stake, capped at 1.0. Not a new measurement — re-packages the same sharp-fair price gap as `best`/`edges_by_book`. Main-line tokens (moneyline, spreads, totals; tennis totals unpublished). A single sharp book (n=1 Pinnacle) is a valid fair reference; soccer and tennis never have a two-book sharp consensus. Gaps ≤ 0 or above 25% (stale-line artifact) are dropped. When `best` is a suppressed MLB moneyline book (DraftKings/FanDuel proven null, or BetMGM/Bet365/BetOnline unscreened), the next eligible book in `edges_by_book` is used. Spreads/totals do not inherit that suppression. Unverified market-consensus estimate — see docs/internal/sports/PREDICTIVE_CLAIM_LADDER.md."""


