class ForecastDriver(TypedDict, total=False):
    id: str
    """Namespaced driver id. Player-prop rows: typically `player.l10_rate` — the recent-form counting-stat rate that fed the Poisson step (also `player.season_rate` when L10 is too thin). Main-line rows would use a different namespace (e.g. a rating or surface split) once a main-line forecast model ships."""
    input: Optional[float]
    """Measured rate/rating behind this driver, in the units native to the underlying model (e.g. 0.27 runs/game, 7.4 strikeouts/start for the prop rate model). This is λ before the Poisson vs the posted line on prop rows."""
    effect: float
    """Signed shift in `p_hit` versus a baseline case on the same line, in probability units. Positive / `direction=up` means this driver lifts the chosen outcome. 0.0 on yardage markets (league means are diluted by backups)."""
    direction: str
    """`up` when `effect` > 0, `down` when `effect` < 0, `neutral` at zero."""


class ForecastWager(TypedDict, total=False):
    event_id: Optional[int]
    """Lumify event ID. Present on the daily slate (`GET /v1/intelligence/forecasts`); omitted on `GET /v1/events/{id}/intelligence` `forecasts[]` (the event is the path)."""
    sport: Optional[str]
    """Sport slug. Slate only."""
    league: Optional[str]
    """League slug, if any. Slate only."""
    commence_time: Optional[str]
    """ISO-8601 UTC scheduled start. Slate only."""
    home_team: Optional[str]
    """Home team display name. Slate only."""
    away_team: Optional[str]
    """Away team display name. Slate only."""
    player: Optional[str]
    """Player display name from the priced line. Null on main-line rows with no player attribution (`bet_type` is a match-level token like OVER/UNDER/ML_DRAW)."""
    player_id: Optional[int]
    """Lumify player ID. Bound by exact / Jr-stripped name match to the priced line. Null on main-line rows with no player attribution."""
    bet_type: Optional[str]
    """Main-line token when this row is a main-line forecast — `ML_P1`/`ML_P2`/`ML_HOME`/`ML_AWAY`/`ML_DRAW`, `SPREAD_P1`/`SPREAD_P2`/`SPREAD_HOME`/`SPREAD_AWAY`, or `OVER`/`UNDER` (same vocabulary as `bets[].bet_type` and `list_ev`). Null on player-prop rows — that's the discriminator between the two row shapes. Tennis sets `ML_P1`/`ML_P2` (moneyline, ranking Bradley-Terry), `SPREAD_P1`/`SPREAD_P2` (game handicap), and `OVER`/`UNDER` (total games — soft-book game-unit lines only, never Pinnacle's set-unit total); other sports are still null here."""
    player_role: Optional[str]
    """`home`/`away` for team sports or `p1`/`p2` for head-to-head sports, set only alongside a non-null `bet_type`. Null for player-prop rows and for match-level main-line tokens (OVER, UNDER, ML_DRAW)."""
    market: str
    """Player-prop rows: prop category — 1:1 counting stats. MLB: strikeouts_pitcher, hits, rbis, runs, strikeouts_batter, hits_allowed, earned_runs, outs_recorded. NFL/NCAAF: passing_yards, rushing_yards, receiving_yards, receptions. NBA/NCAAB: points, rebounds, assists, steals, blocks, threes_made. NHL: goals, hockey_assists, shots_on_goal. Main-line rows (when `bet_type` is set): the main-line family — `h2h`, `spreads`, or `totals`."""
    line: Optional[float]
    """Posted line the model was scored against. Player-prop and `totals` main-line rows: Over/Under number. `spreads` main-line rows: the spread number. Null on `h2h`/moneyline rows."""
    side: Optional[str]
    """Player-prop rows: `over` or `under` — the more likely side given the player's shrunken rate versus `line`. The model always picks one when the line is in range. Null on main-line rows — read the picked outcome from `bet_type` instead."""
    p_hit: float
    """Model probability (0–1) that the picked outcome (`side` on prop rows, `bet_type` on main-line rows) hits. Prop rows: built from the player's shrunken counting-stat rate (Poisson vs the posted Over/Under). Optional `research` may nudge a prop's `p_hit` by at most ±0.03; the chosen side stays the same."""
    interval: List[float]
    """`[lo, hi]` stated band around `p_hit`. Wider when `sufficiency` is low (thin recent sample). A stated evidence band, not a statistical confidence interval."""
    sufficiency: float
    """Evidence weight on 0–1: n / (n + 12), where n is the recent-form game count (typically L10). A player with 10 recent games has sufficiency ≈ 0.45 — about half the rate is player-observed, half prior. The wager still ships at any sufficiency; this field tells you how much of `p_hit` is earned from this player's own boxes."""
    reliability: str
    """Badge on this sport×market cell: `emerging`, `moderate`, `high`, or `informational`. v0 ships `emerging` for every wager; cells promote as a scored history accumulates."""
    conviction: float
    """Board rank key on 0–1: |p_hit − 0.5| × 2 × sufficiency × research multiplier. A 0.76 call on a thin sample ranks below a 0.62 call on a long one. Highest conviction first on the daily slate."""
    model_version: str
    """Scorer version, e.g. `forecast-v0`."""
    selected: bool
    """True when this wager is on the daily board (top conviction, up to 3 per event / 25 on the slate). On `GET /intelligence` the array includes both selected rows and the rest of the event catalog."""
    books: Dict[str, Any]
    """American price for the picked outcome, keyed by bookmaker slug (e.g. `{draftkings: -453}`). Posted market price for the side/bet_type the model picked — use it to see what books are charging for that outcome."""
    drivers: List[ForecastDriver]
    """Signed contributions that moved `p_hit`. Read `input` as the measured rate/rating behind the pick and `effect` as how far it lifts (or lowers) the chosen outcome versus a baseline on the same line."""
    research: Optional[Dict[str, Any]]
    """Optional Deep Research overlay when the background job has written a row for a high-probability wager (`p_hit` ≥ 0.80): `{stance, conviction, note}`. `stance` is `validate` / `neutral` / `invalidate`. `note` is the wager-level why (the fact the model cannot see). Validate / invalidate rows always carry a note. Validate nudges `p_hit` up by at most 0.03 and lifts conviction; invalidate does the reverse. The chosen `side` stays the same. Null means read `p_hit` from the rate model alone — missing research is fail-open, not a 400."""


